    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18721" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fraudātor</span></b> , ōris,
			m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				cheat</i>, <i>deceiver</i>, <i>defrauder</i> (rare but class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">creditorum Trebellius et homo diruptus
					dirutusque,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Phil. 13, 12, 26</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fraudatorum et infitiatorum impudentia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Fl. 20, 48</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">beneficiorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ben. 4, 26</span></i>
			.</div>
